  "title": "Research Collection Punktet Auch 2021 Mit Relevanz Und In Zahlen",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Dominance",
      "text": "Another interesting point to note is that the article with the highest altmetric score back in 2020 was on the subject of climate change. Despite the COVID-19 pandemic, nothing has changed in this regard for 2021. The research report itself also deals with the subject of setting new records – but in a more negative sense: “Increasing probability of record-shattering climate extremes” .\n\nThere is one doctoral thesis that has regularly topped the rankings since the statistics were first recorded: “Eine neue Bestimmung der Moleküldimensionen“ – the groundbreaking 17-page 1905 essay by one of ETH Zurich’s most famous alumni: Albert Einstein."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Groundbreaking",
      "text": "The high level of interest in this article is a strong indicator that the publication of research data is becoming increasingly important and that the publication volume of this type of publication is growing."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Subscribe to Newsletter",
      "text": "Go to the infographic for 2021 in review"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Staffnet",
      "text": "The Research Collection is the publication platform of ETH Zurich. University members can use it to publish academic full texts on an open-access basis, as well as to archive research data or to make these available to the public.\n\nMore than just data – Benefit from know-how #KnowHow – The ETH Library’s infrastructure and tools lead you to your goal."
    }
  ],
